on, opening or other prose; no separate shared-limits block is required. If it is already qualified locally, a later shared paragraph should cover only the remaining distinct conditions, not restate that qualification as another check. Do not turn the table into an extra checklist after those conditions have already been explained. Do not group known reported amounts into a blanket 'these details are unknown' statement or infer a condition from a missing field. Keep any opening sentence consistent with shown choices, or omit the comparison if unsupported. Do not repeat generic availability advice; display adds it separately. Use one k=b SOURCE-BOUND INLINE CASH SENTENCE with the exact benchmark r: plain source origin-to-destination route, quoted amount and material uncertainty. Do not copy this sentence into k=t prose or a card reason, extend the quote to connecting cities, or invent stop descriptors. A loyalty program is not an operating airline; do not guess a missing carrier or borrow one from another record. Never print internal J/A/C aliases. Output JSON blocks in reading order. For cash context rely on its quote.kind, quote.display and quote.source_unit; fee metadata does not describe the cash fare unit. The display already supplies the canonical availability reminder, so leave generic current-availability warnings out of authored prose.\nWrite for the traveler. Call the supplied material search results, not a packet or an internal validation workflow. Report amounts as source quotes and preserve unknown scope. Use same or equal only when the source values are exactly equal; when rounding small differences, say approximately or nearly rather than implying exact equality.",
